# History — closed items' records, kept whole

When an item closes — done, retired or superseded — its triad and its notes move here, with their
folder names unchanged and only their relative links re-pointed, so anything cited by path or by heading
is still found. **History is read, never built from.** A retired item's requirements are the record of
what was tried and withdrawn, not a spec.

| Moved | What | Why it closed |
|---|---|---|
| | *(nothing yet)* | |

What moves, and when:

- a `phase-<id>-<slug>/` triad under `.claude/context/`, when the owner marks its row ✅ `Completed`,
  🟢 `Live` or ⛔ `Retired` and nothing in it is still cited by an open item;
- the roadmap's closed `▶` notes, which go to `.claude/context/roadmap-archive.md` byte for byte;
- a ruled decision, once the item it blocked has closed.

The roadmap row stays, pointing here. Ids are never reused, so a closed item's id keeps meaning what it meant.
